---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { engineeringProjects, supportingProjects } from '../data/engineering-projects';
const base = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/`;
---
<Layout title="Engineering index — Chad Hamilton" description="Evidence, implementation boundaries, and relationships across independent software, AI, automation, and infrastructure projects.">
  <header class="section-pad"><div class="shell"><a class="back-link" href={`${base}#work`}>← Selected work</a><p class="eyebrow">Engineering / October 2026</p><h1>What connects. What works. What remains open.</h1><p class="hero__lede">Independent project work across software development, AI systems, automation, infrastructure, and security boundaries—not a claim of professional employment.</p></div></header>
  <section class="section-pad-sm section-rule"><div class="shell prose"><h2>Read the evidence, not just the label.</h2><p><strong>Verified:</strong> identified execution or test evidence for a stated scope. <strong>Implemented but unverified:</strong> source exists without sufficient current acceptance. <strong>Experimental:</strong> exploratory systems, even where individual tests pass. <strong>Planned:</strong> not implemented and never counted as a delivered capability.</p><p>Verification dates and limitations matter. Historical receipts do not mean a project has passed again today. Weatherful was not located in the bounded workspace audit and is not presented as delivered work.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section-pad section-rule"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Find engineering evidence</p><h2>Choose a technical direction.</h2><div class="engineering-grid">
    <article class="engineering-card"><h3>AI & retrieval</h3><p><a href={`${base}projects/inquiry-engine/`}>Inquiry Engine</a>: retrieval policy, source traces, model processing, and saved investigations.</p></article>
    {engineeringProjects.map(p => <article class="engineering-card"><p class="eyebrow">{p.discipline}</p><h3><a href={`${base}projects/${p.slug}/`}>{p.name}</a></h3><p>{p.summary}</p><p><strong>{p.status}</strong></p></article>)}
    <article class="engineering-card"><h3>Data & cross-platform integration</h3><p><a href={`${base}projects/energy-engine/`}>Energy Engine</a>: read-only health bridge, normalization, provenance, and clear model limitations.</p></article>
  </div></div></section>
  <section class="section-pad section-dark"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Ecosystem relationships</p><h2>Connections with evidence, not implied integrations.</h2><ul class="project-action-list"><li>ICY Reality geometry + Visual Lab signal code → Discovery instruments: direct source reuse.</li><li>Discovery → Luxar: documented bounded native-tool exchange. Upstream tools retain their authorship.</li><li>Health Connect → Kotlin bridge → Energy adapters and state: implemented read-only data boundary.</li><li>Inquiry retrieval → reasoning → SQLite record: historically exercised connected workflow.</li><li>Local AI Lab and Inquiry share infrastructure concerns, not a verified automatic deployment pipeline.</li><li>ORIENT, Generative Reality, and Music Branch Resolver are independent; no shared observation store or media pipeline is implied.</li></ul></div></section>
  <section class="section-pad"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Supporting investigations</p><h2>More work, with its boundaries intact.</h2><div class="engineering-grid">{supportingProjects.map(p => <article class="engineering-card"><h3>{p.name}</h3><p><strong>{p.status}</strong></p><p>{p.scope}</p></article>)}</div></div></section>
</Layout>